From b381e97e89cc6688409b800208546ab93dead710 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 20:20:12 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] audit fixes (2026-08-05 code audit): inject-list, QoS
 CSRF+poll, IP canon, boot-init, delete-tolerance, esc/cleanups

Fixes from docs/CODE-AUDIT-2026-08-05.md (all shared code; fans out to all 5 models):
- C1 reaper_inject.c: add Reaper_Conn/QoSDiag/WiFiPro to reaper_native[] so the
  stock reaper_content.css is NOT injected into these self-themed native pages
  (they still bounce a direct-URL hit into the shell, like Reaper_GK).
- F1 web.c do_reaper_qdiag_cgi: require http_id (mirrors Warden A1-SEC-002) before
  the bdmf_shell popen; Reaper_QoSDiag.asp now sends the token. Stops a cross-site
  GET from forking the diagnostic subprocess.
- Perf web.c/Reaper_QoS.asp: gate the 3s tmctl(x7) poll on document visibility
  (backgrounded tab no longer forks); behaviour identical while visible.
- M1/F2 web.c set_reserve + widen_pool: store the CANONICAL dotted-quad IP, not the
  raw request string (inet_aton accepts octal/hex/short forms, so validated != stored).
- M2 misc.c gen_custom_clientlist_groupid: initialise the malloc'd gvalue buffer
  (was an uninitialised read via find_clientlist_groupid on the first app-grouped entry).
- L2 web.c del_custom_clientlist + api del: parse only enough to compare the MAC
  (>=2 fields) and re-emit the untruncated 'p', so a tuple longer than the parse
  buffer is no longer dropped on delete.
- D2 esc: add ' -> &#39; to the five escapers that omitted it (defence-in-depth;
  text-context so not currently reachable). DC1: drop trafGo's unused mac arg.
  Conn dscpName: remove the no-op ternary arm.

Deliberately NOT changed (documented in the audit): L1 leading-'<' (cosmetic, and
re-touching the just-stabilised set_name RMW isn't worth it) and L3 static snapshot
arrays (latent only; httpd serialises these requests). Verified: make shared + make
httpd exit 0 (no new warnings in edited regions); all 8 edited pages node --check clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
